What this does:

1. As soon as we’ve computed `eventSizeInBytes` (but before falling into the big `if/else if (event.ph === ...)` cascade), we grab all events whose `ph === 'R'`.  
2. We tell the stats machinery that we’ve seen a “marker” event (so it won’t fall through as an instant or duration).  
3. We call `new tr.model.XMarkerAnnotation(...)` with the converted timestamp and push it into `this.model_`.  That annotation will then be rendered in the timeline on the special marker track as a thin vertical line.  
4. We `continue;` to skip the rest of the import logic for those events, preventing them from ever becoming zero-length slices in the “Interactions” lane.  

After applying this patch, your synthetic Lighthouse metrics (which you injected as `ph:'R'`) will show up as proper thin X-markers in DevTools’ timeline UI instead of being drawn as little slices.
